Z||000004||Gold-86SE||02-22-2001||10:39 AM||||<BR>OK guys, I'm confused.<P>I thought that to time the engine (84-86 4-cyl) all you needed to do was ground the diagnostic terminal, connect the timing light to the battery and the #1 plug and point it at the harmonic balancer, and depending on the mark either adavance or retard the distributor.<P>So what gives with the averaging of the #1 and #4 plugs?<P>------------------<BR>84 SE 4.10 4 Speed (Cold and Rain Daily Driver)<BR>85 GT Automatic (Restoration Project)<BR>86 SE 4 Speed (Fair Weather Daily Driver)<BR>87 SC 5 Speed (Not Running, V8 Conversion?)<BR>Please visit my <A HREF="http://www.trifocus.net/~fws/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Work Shop</A>||||reg||1
