Z||000007||Max The Chainsaw||02-23-2001||02:03 PM||||I got a question, what about timing from the coil wire. The timing light will flash on all 4  cyls, but there will only be a mark there for #1 and #4. You'd see both at once and could just set it for 8 degrees.<P>A little trick I learned years ago for setting timing on somewhat worn out v8's.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||862M4inCA||02-24-2001||06:20 PM||||Good point there Max, but every 4 cyl car I've tried to time using the coil wire (since essentially it's going to give you the "firing" time for #1 and #4) give me an erratic number. It doesn't appear to be consistant and the marks "float" anywhere from 4-8 degrees. I've found that timing with just the #1 on the Fiero doesn't quite dial the timing in right which is why it's best to use the averaging method. The ONLY time I did the coil wire method was to get it in the general area I needed, and went from there with the average 8 degree specs.||||reg||1
